Subject: [PATCH] Use the RTD1395 32-bit secondary-core mailbox

The existing SPI firmware releases secondary cores through a 32-bit MMIO
mailbox. Keep the upstream 64-bit protocol for all other boards.

Protocol provenance: Realtek GPL BSP, arch/arm/cpu/armv8/start.S.
See docs/PROVENANCE.md for the pinned source reference and attribution.

--- a/arch/arm/cpu/armv8/start.S
+++ b/arch/arm/cpu/armv8/start.S
@@ -199,7 +199,11 @@
 slave_cpu:
 	wfe
 	ldr	x1, =CPU_RELEASE_ADDR
+#ifdef CONFIG_TARGET_BPI_M4_FC
+	ldr	w0, [x1]
+#else
 	ldr	x0, [x1]
+#endif
 	cbz	x0, slave_cpu
 	br	x0			/* branch to the given address */
 #endif /* CONFIG_ARMV8_MULTIENTRY */
